WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.650
Actual hosted application screenshots
Edited and narrated still states

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.395
BioGraph Steward helps a researcher check what supports a
biological

00:00:08.395 --> 00:00:12.154
claim. We start with a saved research workspace built from

00:00:12.154 --> 00:00:17.122
Pharos, covering ninety-nine human protein targets. Choose the
main real-data

00:00:17.122 --> 00:00:21.454
example. This walkthrough follows one question, its answer, and
the

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.728
evidence behind it.

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:26.452
Read the answer

00:00:26.802 --> 00:00:31.532
The question asks which proteins have a recorded physical
association

00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:35.923
with KRAS. The answer lists fourteen partners. The diagram shows

00:00:35.923 --> 00:00:39.707
one selected path. Open one result, AKT1. The text says

00:00:39.707 --> 00:00:43.896
what STRING reported and gives a source link. Candidate means

00:00:43.896 --> 00:00:48.963
the record still needs review. Physical association can include
membership

00:00:48.963 --> 00:00:52.882
in the same protein complex. It does not establish direct

00:00:52.882 --> 00:00:53.490
binding.

00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:57.254
Inspect one source

00:00:57.604 --> 00:01:01.481
Follow the source link. Read who supplied the record, which

00:01:01.481 --> 00:01:05.229
release it came from, and what the relationship means. We

00:01:05.229 --> 00:01:09.365
check which protein record each source uses, including its full

00:01:09.365 --> 00:01:14.147
sequence. Unmatched identities stay unknown. This does not
guarantee that

00:01:14.147 --> 00:01:18.025
an old assay used the identical protein construct or tissue

00:01:18.025 --> 00:01:22.419
context. STRING already contributes to Pharos, so a second
database

00:01:22.419 --> 00:01:26.361
record is not automatically a second independent experiment.

00:01:28.507 --> 00:01:30.157
Read the measured comparison

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:35.053
What changed shows a measured comparison with published location
labels.

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:40.285
Among thirty-one matching proteins, Pharos recovered forty-one of
fifty-one labels.

00:01:40.285 --> 00:01:45.579
Qualified native annotations recovered forty-four. A separate
check against OpenCell

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:49.938
imaging recovered thirty-one of forty labels instead of thirty,
among

00:01:49.938 --> 00:01:54.983
twenty-three matching proteins. We had already used OpenCell
during development.

00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:59.093
These are coverage gains on known positive labels. Shared sources

00:01:59.093 --> 00:02:02.519
and cell context limit the conclusion. They are not an

00:02:02.519 --> 00:02:06.069
accuracy percentage for every relationship in the graph.

00:02:08.308 --> 00:02:09.958
Understand review and pruning

00:02:10.308 --> 00:02:14.544
The accepted view is empty because no local acceptance decision

00:02:14.544 --> 00:02:19.045
has been made. Fourteen partners remain available to inspect.
Empty

00:02:19.045 --> 00:02:22.289
does not mean there is no evidence. Now open the

00:02:22.289 --> 00:02:27.121
separate TP53 qualification example. Its input had sixteen
thousand nine

00:02:27.121 --> 00:02:32.350
hundred and eighty-five records. Sixteen thousand six hundred and
eighty-seven

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:36.851
remain, with two hundred and ninety-eight excluded because they
use

00:02:36.851 --> 00:02:41.881
obsolete Gene Ontology identifiers. The original records and every
decision

00:02:41.881 --> 00:02:46.978
remain available. Gene Ontology labels protein functions and
locations. This

00:02:46.978 --> 00:02:51.082
rule checks the identifiers. It does not prove the biological

00:02:51.082 --> 00:02:52.472
relationships false.

00:02:54.813 --> 00:02:56.463
Share a traceable result

00:02:56.813 --> 00:03:01.119
Return to the KRAS example. The question's answer download
contains

00:03:01.119 --> 00:03:05.046
this focused summary, its paths and cited evidence. Then open

00:03:05.046 --> 00:03:09.289
Export. The full workspace download keeps the complete saved graph

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:13.659
and source material. A separate graph handoff records every
decision

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:17.712
and preserves the input baseline. The contribution is an answer

00:03:17.712 --> 00:03:22.715
a colleague can inspect and reproduce, with measured reference-
coverage gains.

00:03:22.715 --> 00:03:27.274
We have not established whole-graph scientific accuracy or a
consistent

00:03:27.274 --> 00:03:31.327
gain in graph prediction. An optional NVIDIA Nemotron agent can

00:03:31.327 --> 00:03:34.874
propose a bounded plan. The app checks the allowed tool

00:03:34.874 --> 00:03:39.117
calls before execution. This shared review replays saved data with

00:03:39.117 --> 00:03:40.067
the model off.
